§ `Article 15: a distance is measured in a straight line on a horizontal plane unless the contrary intention appears`

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
      way IS A `Way a distance was measured`
GIVETH A `Distance as measured`
`a distance of` n `metres measured` way MEANS
    `Distance as measured` WITH
        `the distance` IS n
        `the unit` IS "metres"
        `the way it was measured` IS way

#ASSERT `Article 15: the distance as measured is the distance for the purposes of the enactment` `text V1` (`a distance of` 100 `metres measured` `in a straight line on a horizontal plane`) FALSE
